Remove dead code and tighten the README

Full-project sweep: an AST pass over every backend module for unused imports,
unreachable packages and dead assets, then verify by reference.

Removed, each confirmed unreferenced before deletion:
- frontend/components/AlertBanner.tsx and ImageGrid.tsx, plus the five default
  Next.js SVGs in frontend/public (no imports, no references anywhere)
- backend/app/models/, an empty package nothing imports
- backend/tests/_render_e2e.py and _render_showcase.py, both self-described
  throwaway harnesses, and verify_e2e.py, an undocumented duplicate of the
  documented _e2e_local_check.py (which is kept)
- backend/tests/fixtures/real_images/, four JPEGs no test reads; tests synthesise
  their own images through helpers.create_test_image_bytes
- the root .env.example, a partial duplicate of backend/.env.example and
  frontend/.env.example that had already drifted from both

Also removes 31 unused imports across 16 modules, found by AST analysis and
checked against re-exports before removal.

README rewritten from 543 to 286 lines: the oversized ASCII architecture
diagram, the duplicated evaluation box and the long measurement tables are gone,
replaced by a compact pipeline diagram, a providers table, the cross-machine key
troubleshooting table, and honest scope limits. No technical claim was dropped
without moving it to the document that owns it.

Verified: 238 tests pass, tsc clean, next build clean.

